# v40 per-project wiring for httpcloak. Written by /v40:setup; nothing else
# writes this file. Shell assignments only — the prose that explains them lives
# in .v40/wiring.md beside it.
#
# Precedence: an exported environment variable beats this file, and this file
# beats shipctl.sh's built-in defaults. Nothing recorded here takes a per-run
# decision away from the operator.
#
# Knobs not listed here keep shipctl.sh's built-in default on purpose: a value
# nobody measured is worse than the default.

# See .v40/wiring.md — `-short` is a correctness choice, not a speed one.
SHIPCTL_SUITE_CMD="go test -short ./..."

# From `shipctl.sh setup-check --fingerprint`, so this value and the one later
# compared against it are produced by the same code.
SHIPCTL_CI_FINGERPRINT="2c4d6c88ca7bd3ca18eb1c12d503184fb7a45c48c1f23228ca7977153eacef70"

# SHIPCTL_CHECKS_REQUIRED is deliberately unset. This repository has no CI, and
# that was verified against the server rather than inferred — see .v40/wiring.md.
# Unset keeps checks-wait reporting checks-not-observed and letting the merge
# proceed, which is the correct outcome when there is nothing to observe.
